# Both images build from the repo root (the pnpm workspace is the build
# context), so this one file covers them. Keeping it lean matters twice over:
# it shrinks what Docker uploads as context, and it keeps host-only artefacts
# from shadowing what the build produces inside the image.

# Never ship dependency trees from the host -- they are platform-specific
# (argon2 is a native module) and would silently override the ones installed
# inside the image for the target architecture.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output, regenerated inside the image
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage

# Secrets. The real .env lives on the host and is injected at runtime by
# Dokploy; .env.example stays because it documents the contract.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
.husky
.claude

# Editor/OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local-only tooling that has no bearing on a production image
docker-compose.yml
**/*.md

# Tests never run inside the production image -- CI already gates them
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
apps/api/test
